{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/454055-liberti\u00e9-\u2022-\u00e9galiti\u00e9-\u2022-vitae-actual-play","id":454055,"title":"Liberti\u00e9 \u2022 \u00c9galiti\u00e9 \u2022 Vitae - Actual Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-23T04:39:04-07:00","id":454055,"title":"Liberti\u00e9 \u2022 \u00c9galiti\u00e9 \u2022 Vitae - Actual Play","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A city on the edge of chaos, Paris is a capital of squalor and suffering as the 18th Century draws to a close. While for hundreds of years the regular procession of plagues kept the peasant population in check there has been no great sickness in generations, and the numbers of the underclass swells in the city. Now Paris is home to almost 650,000 people, and only a bare ten thousand are of the first and second estates, the clergy and the nobility. The rest call the third their home and make up the peasantry. As the population has swollen the balance of production and consumption has become ever more unstable and dangerous, the poor roads and tracks making it impossible to import grain to the city at anything other than extortionate prices, and so the populace relies totally on the agriculture of the city surrounds themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Only the regulation of bread prices keeps the city from starving and even then, when a bad harvest occurs, the peasantry riots nearly tearing the city apart, lynching bakers, stealing bread and burning down buildings that have stood for half a millennium. The clergy and nobility pay no taxes and take all that they want, and are impeachable in the courts of the land. The young king and queen, Louis XVI and Marie Antoinette, luxuriate in the palace of Versailles far from the heavy masses, totally isolated from the pain and suffering of the lower classes. King Louis, though most incompetent, refuses to appoint important ministerial figures claiming his right to rule the country directly and believing that it is his duty to do so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">His father, and his father's father, wasted the riches of France on a series of petty wars and disputes, the lands and monies of France slowly eaten away. The rich have gotten richer, and the poor poorer as they are squeezed more and more to pay for the excesses of the first and second estates. The people call for a three house parliament to represent the common man, but such pleas are ignored. France teeters on bankruptcy, a matter which is not helped by Marie Antoinette's lavish spending, and the vast sums Louis sends to aid the American Wars of Independence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It is June 1787, and the hungry gap is beginning, when the harvests are yet to be brought in but the grain stores are running low. Bread is scarce and the city boils and fumes in the heat and the poverty, a powder keg that somehow never explodes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As above, so below.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The three estates of the dead struggle against each other just as the kine do. The nobility of the night and the followers of Longinus claim the first and second estates, with the rest relegated to the third. Those kindred who are not embraced into noble lines, or who cannot worm their way into the church, are left to rot, forced to pay the blood taxes of the nobles and given nothing in return. A bare handful of bloodlines hold all the power and the rest scramble to just survive.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As the kine population bloats as do the leeches that feed from them, hundreds of the dead hanging like parasites from the city. With so many deaths through crime, starvation and a thousand other evils, the peasantry of the city are a never-ending buffet for the kindred whose predations are always overlooked. Yet fury and resentment ferments amongst the downtrodden masses of the dead, just as they do amongst the living. The kindred might have blood aplenty but they lack safety in a city which burns on a yearly basis, and which is ripped apart by riots almost monthly. They look at the sturdy chambers and manors of their betters and then plot amongst themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Just as the pamphleteers of the mortal world fuel the ever-encroaching revolution, so do the radicals of the dead urge their fellows to action. The name Emmanuel Baptiste Carth is upon the lips of the many, and soon they will be bound together into a great movement whose actions can only result in blood and fire.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I\u2019ve been running World of Darkness for almost a decade, and of all the roleplaying games I\u2019ve played and run (there have been many) it\u2019s the one I return to again and again. When Blood and Smoke (now Requiem 2nd Edition) came out I desperately wanted to run something using it. I came up with the concept for a game charting the early days of the Carthians from their radical roots in Paris during the last part of the 18th Century through the bloody revolution that gripped that city and, perhaps, concealed a similarly bloody revolution amongst the dead. I ran the game and it was a great success but unfortunately it was cut short \u2013 I had to move cities for my work and my gaming group was left behind.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Well, now I have a new group and I think it\u2019s time to celebrate a rebooting of this setting with an Actual Play. I'll be posting up some more introductory information shortly, and then the first three sessions of play after that. Once that's done new sessions of play will go up on Wednesdays most weeks.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T04:41:57-07:00","id":454073,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><u>Themes</u></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I\u2019m going to take a leaf out of DaveB\u2019s Actual Play threads here (which are just balls-out amazing) and be upfront about the themes I\u2019m teasing out of Requiem for the purposes of this game.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Everyone is Alone Together</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I sometimes joke that Requiem should really be called High-Functioning Psychopaths the RPG and though that\u2019s a little overegged as a concept, it\u2019s not that far off the mark. Every kindred has a beast inside them, this monster that wants to just play with the world. It used to be out and out bestial in first edition, but since Blood and Smoke came along it\u2019s found a little more nuance. The bestial triad makes me sit up and pay attention because it\u2019s a great framework for what kindred are like, really like, at the core of themselves. They\u2019re equal parts pack animal, solitary predator and fucked up human being. I don\u2019t want to forget that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The thing is that vampires define themselves by their connections with others, but those connections are always hollow \u2013 they might find scraps of loyalty and brotherhood amongst themselves but in the end fraternity is a lie amongst the dead. You might fool yourself into thinking you\u2019re still a human being for a little longer than the others but you\u2019re just not, and that\u2019s\u2026 well, not OK, but that\u2019s a thing. You can\u2019t fight your way out of that. Vampires just don\u2019t have the ability to trust anyone else anymore, especially other vampires, and so it\u2019s all about finding the ways to interact socially without just ripped each other\u2019s faces off. That\u2019s why kindred form such complex organisations and structure. Because you\u2019re right not to trust each other.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Predator or Prey</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Vampires are predators. That\u2019s just a fact that bleeds through every part of the book when you read Requiem, and which plays off nearly half the mechanics in it. Worse, when your food supply is something that everyone has, you can\u2019t even switch off that instinct with anyone. Whenever you meet another vampire you\u2019re categorising them into something I want to eat or something that might eat me (or both). It\u2019s not as blunt as in first edition (where predatory aura was a like a sledgehammer to social situations), but it\u2019s omnipresent. Masques and Dirges are about working out your place in the pecking order, your predatory niche. Status is about who gets to eat who. Blood Potency is about who\u2019s got the bigger teeth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Which is funny, in a sort of awful way, when you start thinking about the Carthians. Because the radicals in the city of Paris genuinely believe in \u00c9galiti\u00e9, in making society equal and fairer, to stop there being people at the top and people at the bottom, monsters at the top and monsters at the bottom. The problem is that you can strip away all the pomp and circumstance, all the centuries of rotting power, but you won\u2019t ever get that equality because every single part of your being makes you divide people into above me and below me. That\u2019s what lashing out is about proving \u2013 that you\u2019re the one doing the eating.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Die Free</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Kindred need those structures, those complex organisations and associations because otherwise their basic social natures will break out and those natures ain\u2019t pretty. But that doesn\u2019t mean any of the dead actually like those structures, and those kindred who do badly out of them are going to like them least of all. That\u2019s what the radicals really want of course, to stop being on the shitty end of the current system. The problem is, instead of trying to beat the system and get on top they think they can just get rid of the system. For reasons I\u2019ve already covered, that\u2019s a bad idea all round, and almost certainly won\u2019t work.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The kindred of Paris who are scrabbling to form this new movement want Libert\u00e9, they want freedom from the structures and systems in place. The problem is none of them can agree on what should replace it and all they can agree on is tearing what\u2019s there at the moment down. That\u2019s a recipe for disaster and though the players might realise it the characters are too trapped and desperate to think ahead to what the domain will look like when (or if) they get what they want. They want to be free, but free in vampires is just the worst idea ever. So they\u2019ll forge their own chains as they go along, just like real people trying to have a revolution do. You ever thought about what the reign of terror would look like with a dead man at the helm?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The kindred at the bottom of the pile really are trapped though, in a way few vampires ever are. The system of tenancy, barony and corv\u00e9e means that their requiems are very hard indeed, and that they are constantly at the whim of others. Breaking out of those traps would be freedom of a sort, regardless of the consequences.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Blood Bonds and Blood Oaths</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Because when it comes down to it, really when you strip it all away, it\u2019s all about blood. Thick, rich dark ruddy blood, pooling in your mouth and your dead veins. You\u2019re bound by your blood, not just through the vinculum but also through family, your kinship with your lineage and your clan pulling you in lots of different directions.at once. That\u2019s before you pledge your allegiance to something or someone else, giving your blood oath of service (or at least loyalty). We know that loyalty is hollow so all that\u2019s left standing is the blood.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">But there are too many ties for that to be easy. You have allegiance to your clan, your family, your estate, your faction, your coterie, your liege\u2026 to everyone and everything with a stake in your requiem. You can\u2019t make all of those people, all of those organisation, your priority, and you sure as hell can\u2019t please them all. So you have to make choice about which way you go, who you stay loyal to and who you betray. You also need to decide if those decision are based on your own survival, that blood that drives you, or if you try to cleave to something greater, some noble cause.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You can find a link to the full setting document here: </span></span><a href=\"http://1drv.ms/1yRYm1l\" target=\"_blank\">http://1drv.ms/1yRYm1l</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T04:48:23-07:00","id":454076,"title":"","content":"<b><u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Player Characters</span></u></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Just a brief blurb for everyone, as I want to reveal their character through play rather than just giving you the details up front. Sorry about that. Characters are built on base dots + 10xp, I will append proper sheets when I remember.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Agathe Saint-Simon Moreau</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">An illegitimate daughter of the youngest son of a minor noble, Agathe was barely noble in the first place and her fall from grace has done her position few favours. Though given some education as a child she soon rebelled even on those minor restrictions; she adopted masculine dress even though she doesn\u2019t pretend to be male, rebelling even against the strictures of her gender. When she was embraced she hunted down and killed her mortal father and his legitimate family as an expression of fury against him, and the resultant chaos forced her underground, where she has stayed since. Recently she has begun working as a tough in a brothel, dealing with customers who get too rough with the girls (who double as her herd). Nosferatu of the sprawling Moreau brood, she favours direct action over cunning plots when circumstances allow. She currently makes her haven in Montparnasse and her regent is Georgine Rome.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 LaPointe</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Embraced by the since executed Daeva noble Christophe LaPointe, Andre was inducted into the Second Estate. He made that transition relatively smoothly, despite being of the tender age of eleven at embrace, since he was of mortal noble stock and took to command well. When Christophe was condemned to final death for treason against Le Requin (the Prince), however, he was exiled to the rougher areas of the city and forced to accept Comtesse Giselle Rome as his regent, being granted the right to remain in Fauborg Saint-Germain. He\u2019s a member of the Children\u2019s Crusade and a deadly kindred duellist, but he still retains many of his noble connections giving him a big social advantage. He\u2019s also inherited his sire\u2019s bloodline which gives him the ability to create vinculums in others not to himself, but to ideals or duties.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Benoit Moreau</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Found dead in an alley by a ghoul of the Moreau brood, Benoit was taken to the bloodline\u2019s holdings before being subjected to the post-mortem embrace by Phillipe Moreau. Why the patriarch decided to do this, is unclear, and Benoit is a little fuzzy on the details from just before and just after his death. Quick-witted and extremely nimble, he ran with the gangs of street children before he became kindred, and keeps in contact with them now. A thief beyond anything else he\u2019s got a good mix of skills and is something of a soft touch in a coterie of heavy hitters. He lives in Montparnasse with his extended family, and though his liege lord is technically Georgine Rome, but he takes most of his instruction from his sire. He is also a token member of the Children\u2019s Crusade, which is how he first met Andr\u00e9, but he\u2019s never put must investment in the covenant.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel LeClaire</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ex-musketeer (and still bitter about their disbandment), Gabriel LeClaire is a rough and ready kindred mercenary from the Le Garde du Sang bloodline (a group of ex-Invictus kindred who feel they were betrayed by their former covenant). He\u2019s honourable and trustworthy, but more because he stakes his reputation on it than anything else, and he\u2019s a little na\u00efve about the way in which the world works. More wearied soldier than just a common thug, he\u2019s physically capable but with a solid physical background including horse riding and survival skills. He\u2019s also socially quite adept, but sometimes a little tactless. Daeva and a member of the Third Estate only; he doesn\u2019t officially have a liege lord, but instead is employed on a temporary basis by Comte Courtmanche making his haven in the Quartier Latin.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Remy Fergris</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Something of an outsider, Remy is of French extraction but spent most of his mortal life in Algiers in one of the recently established French colonies. A military engineer by trade, he\u2019s a good all-rounder with a broad range of physical and mental skills, and even a dabbling of social capability too. He\u2019s a member of the Gangrel Fergris bloodline which means his vitae hardens into iron when spilt, a property that gives him a long of problem solving flexibility and nasty tricks in a violent situation. He\u2019s a member of L\u2019Academie du Serpent and so will potentially get access to coils (though he\u2019s low down the ladder right now and hasn\u2019t picked up expertise in any of the Mysteries). He also doesn\u2019t have a formal liege but is theoretically under the dominion of Comte Courtmanche, making his haven in the Quartier Latin.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T04:53:57-07:00","id":454078,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I\u2019m following DaveB\u2019s format to the letter, so expect these sections to be out of character, behind the curtain asides. Unfortunately the player of Agathe was sick and couldn\u2019t make the first two sessions, but she\u2019ll appear later on.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">1.1 \u201cCity of Lights\u201d</span></u></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">June, 1787</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 Lapointe is waiting in the parlour of Comtesse Giselle Rome, his liege lord and baron, who has requested his presence that evening on a matter of urgency. With little choice but to present himself he\u2019s waiting nervously. Giselle opens with some flattery and small talk, praising him for his loyalty and restrain, before launching into the meat of the matter: a man has been murdered in Les Invalides and it looks like it might be a masquerade breach. She makes a few carefully-judged insult/compliments about his (previous) noble heritage that has now gone to wrack and ruin, and sends him on his way with the promise that this task would pay off his Corv\u00e9e for the forthcoming year.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">In the domain of Paris all common kindred are forced to pay a yearly \u201crent\u201d to their baron as payment for living on their territory. It was written in pretty much as a blatant way of hooking PCs into situations they don\u2019t really want to be a part of.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Meanwhile in Montparnasse, Benoit Moreau is being entertained by his sire Phillipe Moreau who is the Patriarch of his brood, and who is trying to put the thief at his ease with his usual rough charm. He appeals to familial loyalty and duty and his young prot\u00e9g\u00e9 is more than happy to acquiesce to his request. Put simply, in order to curry favour with the nobility, Phillipe would like Benoit to head over to the tannery in Les Invalides and see if he can help investigate this murder. He\u2019s told to work with the kindred who arrive there.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">The setup is a little blunt at this point, but I didn\u2019t want to waste any time. We\u2019d already established some connections between the characters beforehand so the coterie can naturally come together \u2013 Benoit and Remy have run into each other before through Remy\u2019s touchstone (a young orphan street girl) who Benoit knows through his connections with the group of street kids that live in the slums.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel and Remy are currently in conversation with Comte Courtmanche, who tells them that to keep the peace and ensure they are not disturbed in the Quartier Latin it would be good if Gabriel and Remy could help look into a potential masquerade breach for him. \u201cAfter all,\u201d he tells them, \u201cit\u2019s best if we can stay on everyone\u2019s good side, and a threat to the masquerade is a threat to us all\u201d. Remy and the Comte have a short conversation about who will take over his research in L\u2019Academie du Serpent whilst he\u2019s investigating the murder, and he passes off some of his work to a young kindred called Jennifer.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 arrives first, running through the crowded city (still bustling with people just after dusk) with wild abandon that fits his apparent 11 years of age. He stops a few dozen yards down the street from the tannery which he can see piercing the moonlit sky in the distance, judging the situation on the street. There are a lot of mortals milling around here \u2013 people selling flowers, someone peddling black ribbons in a hopeful if slightly indelicate way, and a large group of people huddling together just outside the tannery whispering amongst themselves. He judges the crowd and guesses that the mortal authorities, the marshals who keep order in the city, have not yet arrived at the scene. It seems the call to action was swift indeed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Remy arrives next as he\u2019s taken the shortcut of climbing up to the roofs and running across the district well above the ground. He reaches the edge of the roof and looks down at the street, noticing Andr\u00e9 standing there below. There\u2019s a momentary pause and then he clocks the little noble boy, dressed in a slightly shabby blue suit, as kindred; something in the stance, in the way he holds himself and the lack of movement in his chest and face gives Andr\u00e9 away as not being amongst the living. Andr\u00e9 looks up and notices Remy and the same thing happens in reverse \u2013 as ex-soldier makes his way down back to street level Andr\u00e9 moves towards him so they can meet up and talk.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It\u2019s not long before Gabriel and Benoit arrive, not having taken quite such a hectic pace to reach their goal. They know the other two and soon the coterie-to-be is in conversation about their next move, having shared their instructions from their various authority figures.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">This was a great little scene of introductory roleplay that I can\u2019t do justice to \u2013 the dynamic of the group really clicked almost immediately. Andr\u00e9 takes a position of authority, even though the two adult-appearing kindred might take their age difference as defining the mechanic. The two military men stick together, following Andr\u00e9\u2019s lead, whilst Benoit soon takes his own direction.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Benoit disappears around the back of the buildings looking for alternative access to the tannery, trusting to his slight frame and practiced stealth to hide him from view. The other three make their way through the crowd (avoiding getting too close to the brazier that a small group are warming their hands on) and head to the door of the tannery itself, Andr\u00e9 taking the lead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A woman leans in the doorway, clearly barring entry to the tannery itself. She\u2019s about thirty and sort of pretty in a worn way, clearly the recipient of a hard life but still trying to make an effort: sloppily applied makeup marks her face, but has been smeared by tear streaks on her face. As the group approach she wearily holds up a hand: \u201cPlease young master, madame and monsieur cannot be intruded upon until the marshals arrive.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 barely misses a bit and tells her with perfect confidence that they are in fact from the marshals office, and have been hired as thief-takers in order to investigate the murder. She looks surprised but ushers them inside, glad things are finally happening. Andr\u00e9 begins to talk to her whilst Remy and Gabriel climb the stairs to find the body itself, passing a rather less attractive, older woman on the landing as they go, and heading into the back bedroom. Andr\u00e9 begins to talk to the woman about what has happened and has found that the tanner is Henry Capet, whilst she is his mistress Lucille. Apparently Henri\u2019s death was a double blow to Henri\u2019s wife Claire, as she discovered not only that he had died, but had been unfaithful. \u201cI fear I may still be in shock,\u201d Lucille confesses to Andr\u00e9, \u201cfor I saw the whole thing and I cannot tell you what horror it was.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">A social challenge began at this point as Andr\u00e9 begins to pump Lucille for information \u2013 the fruits of his labour will be revealed later on.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Meanwhile, Benoit has made his way to the rear of the tannery, scaled the fence, made his way across the tanner\u2019s yard and up the rear of the tanner\u2019s house, finding the bedroom where the body has been placed on the bed with ease. He crouches over the bed and examine the dead made: corpulently fat, pale almost waxen flesh where he has been exsanguinated, and with evidence of being badly beaten as well. In one place white bone pushes through his arm exposing it to the air. It is in this pose that Remy and Gabriel find him as they make their way through in a more conventional fashion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Remy steps over to the corpse and begins to examine him, relying on his experience with field surgery from when he was in the army, and notes that the corpse almost certainly died from trauma, rather than blood loss. He notes the strikes and breaks on the body don\u2019t match a blunt implement, but more just unarmed blow of incredible force. Giving the dead man a little more of a general look over, Gabriel notes what looks like dried blood around his mouth, and the two of them arrive at a rough time of death \u2013 about three hours previously.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A knock at the door stops them in their tracks, and Benoit dives under the bed to hide as Andr\u00e9, followed by Lucille, enter the room. Lucille is in tears and Andr\u00e9 leads her mercilessly to the bed, and shows her the brutal wounds on the body \u2013 \u201cCan you see why, when faced with horror like this, the mind might rebel?\u201d She cries a little but shakes her head saying \u201cYoung master, I promise, she was no figment of the imagination, but as real as you or eye. She was faster than a person should be, young master, and she beat my beloved to death with her bare hands without breaking a sweat.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Guessing what Andr\u00e9 is up to, Remy chimes in, and begins to explain in somewhat gruesome detail the extend of Henri\u2019s injuries. Lucille begins to break down in tears but shakes her head, \u201cI know it is terrible, but I know what I saw.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Andr\u00e9 has started a new social challenge here, convincing Lucille that she has had a breakdown of sanity in the face of Henri\u2019s murder, in an attempt to explain away the overtly supernatural nature of the killer. The challenge started well but faltered badly, and bringing her up here was a last ditch attempt to get her to cave.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel steps in and informs Lucille rather a little too baldly that she is clearly hysterical and should be ashamed of herself for denying it, and she slaps him in her hysteria. For a moment the room crystallises and the kindred freeze, waiting to see what will happen\u2026 but Gabriel controls his urge to frenzy and apologies to her. Sensing that this is getting away from them, Andr\u00e9 make a bold decision.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">At this point the players were getting desperate to contain the potential breach of the masquerade: they had no disciplines or other powers that might have convinced her otherwise, and the social challenge was floundering. They began to discuss how they would deal with it if they had to kill her, but they were, understandably, reluctant.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 puts a hand on Lucille\u2019s arm and then flickers, a strange sort of juddering and in a moment is over by the door. The woman screeches and Andr\u00e9, keeping his cool, merely looks at her and say: \u201cWhat is the matter?\u201d That\u2019s the last straw and in tears she runs past the young vampire sobbing that her mind must be broken and she cannot be trusted.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">The discovery that Celerity didn\u2019t just make you move faster but made that movement unpleasant and overtly supernatural made Andr\u00e9\u2019s player cackle with pleasure, and this scheme was hatched without any input by the rest of the group \u2013 it was a risky gamble, but I liked it enough to reward the attempt. Andr\u00e9 did take a detachment check for this vicious little escapade, however, dropping down to Humanity 5.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Remy and Gabriel begin to scold Andr\u00e9 for endangering the masquerade further, but relent when he points out that the situation was already getting away from them. He goes on to tell them that Lucille had witnessed a woman \u2013 tall, thin and dressed in dirty white rags \u2013 burst through the door about half an hour before sunset, screaming incoherently. She had moved to Henri, clearly consumed with hatred, and began to attack him \u2013 Lucille had run thinking that Henri would be able to take care of himself and fearing for her own safety, only to be knocked aside as the woman rushed past her. When she checked on Henri he was dead. The woman had screamed only one intelligible phrase: \u201cHe will suffer!\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">At this point Benoit pipes up, peering at the corpse again. \u201cIsn\u2019t it a potentially bad sign if he has blood around his mouth, but it\u2019s not come from a wound of his that I can see?\u201d The group quickly reform to look at the body again, and begin to discuss the possible implications \u2013 Gabriel tastes a little of the blood on the dead man\u2019s lips and announces it to be vitae, probably from a Ventrue. The implications are unsettling and, fearing him rising as a revenant, begin to plan on how they\u2019re going to sneak the body out of the house.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">We ran out of time at this point\u2026 to be continued.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T04:54:35-07:00","id":454079,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><u>1.2 \u201cBeneath Your Feet\u201d</u></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">June, 1787</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Without saying a word to the rest of the group, Benoit walks over to a chair, snaps of a leg and, with his knife, carves a very serviceable stake. He passes it to Gabriel in silence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Still under the guide of representatives of the Marshalry, Remy elects to go and speak to the widow and explain that they\u2019ll be taking the body away to let some learned men at L\u2019Universitie examine it, and promises to have her back as soon as possible \u2013 a week at the outside. When he later explains this promise to the rest of the group he receives a nod from Benoit and blank looks from Andr\u00e9 and Gabriel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">It is decided that this total lack of feeling on the part of Gabriel is worth a detachment check, which Gabriel passes. Andr\u00e9 is far too embittered for this to pose a risk to his Humanity.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Whilst Remy is speaking to the wife, Benoit slips back out the window and goes to \u201cacquire\u201d a cart they can use to transport the body. He finds a trundle cart in an alley nearby where a sausage-seller has set up his tray and, unnoticed due to his use of Obfuscate, he quickly removes it and brings it round in a loop to outside the tannery, just as if he\u2019d brought it from elsewhere.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 uses the opportunity to go downstairs and examine the scene of the crime, to see if he can find any leads. The back room where the murder occurred is in disarray \u2013 furniture turned over, part of the plaster on one way torn out in hunks, and smear of blood and hair across the floor in one place. The back door, which leads to the tanner\u2019s yard, is torn asunder, splinters of wood littering the room. Andr\u00e9 heads outside into the darkness of the yard, and stops for a moment to consider his next step.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">This was the first time that vampiric senses and the difficulties of operating in darkness arose. Andr\u00e9\u2019s player decided the penalties were worse than the inconvenience of finding some light source.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Crossing the yard swiftly he heads into the tannery proper and finds just the thing: a mesh-covered lamp which will provide light without risking either ignition of the tanner\u2019s fumes or too much exposure to flame. He takes the lamp and heads out into the street, pushing his blood to call out to those around him, and luring a woman towards him.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">That was Andr\u00e9 activating Majesty 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">He bats his eyelashes at the woman and does his best to look like an adorable lost child. \u201cAre you lost, little sir?\u201d she asks him, and he shakes his head. \u201cNo Madame, but I sorely need your help. Could you light this lamp for me, I fear I don\u2019t quite know how.\u201d Swayed by the call of his vitae she smiles and takes the lamp from him, lighting it easily (and Andr\u00e9 takes a sharp step backwards as she does).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cLet me help you. Where are you trying to go?\u201d she asks him, and though he tries to discourage her subtly, she follows him into the tanner\u2019s yard carrying the lamp for him. Losing patience, he tells her: \u201cI am on a private errand, I really cannot say. Thank you for your help, but it would be best if you went.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dismissed her face falls and her body slumps, but she nods dutifully and turns, leaving the yard. \u201cShe better not have mucked up the prints\u201d mutters Andr\u00e9 to himself, the childlike persona falling away in an instant. He begins to use the light from his lamp to search for tracks in the muddy yard to try and determine which direction the assailant came from.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Upstairs, Gabriel stands over the corpse, tossing the stake from hand to hand.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Having concluded his discussion with the widow, Remy heads into the tanner\u2019s yard to help Andr\u00e9 investigate the scene and, with his enhanced sense, he quickly spots some faint prints leading over to the back of the tannery where heavy basement doors lie open, a dark cellar opening up at the bottom of a short flight of stairs. For a moment Andr\u00e9 and Remy stare at each other, willing the other to be the first to go down and investigate. \u201cI should wait here with the lamp,\u201d says Andr\u00e9, \u201cso I don\u2019t spoil your night vision.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Instead Remy checks around him for mortal witnesses and, seeing none, pushes his blood to shift and change, his body twisting until he possesses a sense he did not before \u2013 the echolocation of a bat. With a short sharp noise he sounds out the cellar below, finding it empty except for shelves and crates and, in the corner hidden behind a large crate, a rough-hewn entrance way to a passage. He concludes instantly that it is an entrance to the necropolis, and almost certainly where the kindred who killed the tanner came from.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The pair head back inside and Gabriel and Remy collect the body (by this point wrapped in a sheet) and take it outside to the waiting handcart that Benoit has collected. They discuss in hushed tones where they\u2019re going to take it and decide on L\u2019Academie du Serpent, as there are people there they might be able to trust with watching over it. They make their way through the streets to Le Quartier Latin, and Benoit and Andr\u00e9 wait whilst the other two deposit the body into the care of Jennifer, the Serpent who took over Remy\u2019s research whilst he was busy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Arriving back into the cool night air and are planning to head back to the Tannery entrance of the Necropolis when, his blood still up from earlier, Andr\u00e9 suggests a little contest to see who can reach their fastest. Gabriel immediately agrees, his blood up, and the others are goaded into participating and they clamber up to a rooftop to begin.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Gabriel has the Competitive condition on him at the moment, so this was perfectly in keeping with his current mental state.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 immediately lashes out a foot to try and trip Remy, who nimbly hops over it and begins running at a steady loping base, his experience with parkour giving him an advantage over the rooftops. Andr\u00e9, set a little behind after his attempt to cheat goes awry, is also highly skilled in this kind of movement, and sets a fast pace. Gabriel, however, is the real monster here, using his vast physical prowess and disciplines to pull ahead of the other two as he runs at full pelt across the city. Benoit merely waits for the other three to move away before sliding back down to ground level, finding the nearest necropolis entrance and popping inside.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cWho are you then?\u201d the burly watchmen on the entrance asks him. Benoit nods his head and says \u201cBenoit, of the Moreau.\u201d The heavyset man sniffs at Benoit then nods. \u201cFair enough. Off you go.\u201d And steps aside to let the little Nosferatu through.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As they leave the Latin Quarter the three kindred on the rooftops begin to seriously gain speed. Les Invalides has broader buildings and now pure speed plays more part, and Gabriel, whose strength far outstrips his opponents, finds himself drawing further and further ahead. Benoit, meanwhile, runs as fast as he can along his much shorter, easy route, and approaches his destination. As a Nosferatu he knows all of the shortcuts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The trio above reach the tanner\u2019s yard and are presented with a choice \u2013 to jump down from the roof or to climb down and spend a little more time doing so. Their blood pumping, all of them choose the former, and Andr\u00e9 and Remy launch themselves to the ground, hitting and rolling with only moderate injury (Andr\u00e9 snaps his ankle, but simply shakes it out and keeps running). Gabriel, his beast screaming at him to win, pushes his vitae into his muscles and throws himself up and out from the building. He flies through the air and crashes down and through the wooden doors covering the basement, his shin bone slamming up through his skin, dark vitae spraying across his face and chest, and onto the walls. He groans and pulls himself up, vitae knitting the wounds back together as he wrenches the bones into place gain, and he staggers into the basement to claim his victory.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">As he had just won a contest in which someone reached a breaking point (him, for suffering injury that would hospitalise a mortal), he resolves the Competitive condition. Which is relief for everyone involved.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Benoit arrives from inside the necropolis only second later, and Andr\u00e9 and Remy catch up only a few seconds after that, Andr\u00e9 fuming at losing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Benoit notes that there was no kindred guarding this entrance to the necropolis \u2013 it must be one of those which is simply concealed from view, rather than one which is actively watched. They take stock for a moment and then, armed with Andr\u00e9\u2019s gas lamp for illumination, head into the caves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel takes over tracking the kindred who entered through here, and quickly identifies two sets of tracks laid over each other \u2013 one coming out of the necropolis, and one going in. They follow the tracks deep into the network of tunnels, using Benoit\u2019s limited knowledge where Gabriel\u2019s tracking breaks down, picking up the path the best they can as they go. Eventually they reach a place where the tracks diverge- they can either head in the direction she came from, or where she went to. The decision is a matter of debate for a few minutes, but in the end cowardice prevails and they follow the tracks of where she came from \u2013 \u201cto learn more about her before we try to apprehend her.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The tracks leads every-deeper into the necropolis, the twists and turns confusing the group as they desperately try to keep on target. They clamber down one sheer slope, and then a few minutes later wade through thigh-deep water (chest-deep for Andr\u00e9 and Benoit). Andr\u00e9 notes that the water is tidal, and could rise further yet \u2013 almost certainly drawn from the Seine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">After exiting the water, Gabriel is working more by guesswork than real evidence of their target\u2019s passage, and brings the group to a halt with the admission that he honestly has no idea where they are headed. They notice directions cut into the wall, but they are all in kindred cant, and none of them are part of the cacophony. Benoit takes the lead and, working on gut instinct and experience of travelling underground, begins to take them into more well-travelled tunnels, rising back towards the surface and away from the confusing labyrinth of the depths.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel and Andr\u00e9 hear it first \u2013 a faint whistling in the distance, the lilt of a tune being performed by someone with no need to use their lungs to breath. Even from this distance they know the tiny clues that speak of one of the dead. Andr\u00e9 draws his rapier and Gabriel shrugs lose his buckler and sabre, though fighting with them in these corridors would be dangerous, for they are tight and trapping. The other two alerted Remy places his hand on the hilt of his sword, but does not draw, and Benoit simply steps back out of notice of the others, his presence disappearing as he exerts his blood to activate Obfuscate.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In the distance in the gloom, they group watch as a man turns the corner into the tunnel where they are stood and, whistling, approaches the party. He seems perfectly at ease. As he approaches they can see his face is oddly shaped on one side, almost like it was wax that had melted a little, and waves of foul stench break over them, filling their senses. He is almost dripping in what seems to be sewerage, his hair slicked down with effluence. He pauses perhaps five yards from the group and raises his hand in greeting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cWhat\u2019s your purpose down here strangers? You\u2019re intruding on territory not your own.\u201d The group share glances and Andr\u00e9 says \u201cWe\u2019re looking for someone.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cLooking for someone\u2026 looking for someone. None of yous smells like kin, so what right you got to be looking for someone?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel raises his eyebrows and says \u201cWe\u2019re travelling with a member\u2026\u201d and turns to find Benoit nowhere in sight. \u201cWhere has the little shit gone to now?\u201d Remy mutters to himself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cOh ho,\u201d the newcomer guffaws, \u201cit seems your guide is not as confident as you seem to be of his company. And who are yous then, who are yous if you ain\u2019t got a Nosferatu to vouch for you?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The group introduce themselves. The newcomer (who can only be a Favager, one of a Nosferatu brood in the city) laughs at the name Lapointe, and shakes his head and tuts as Remy and Gabriel introduce themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cOh dear oh dear. Two foreigners and a stuck up nob, ay? Not healthy for you to be wandering down here in the dark.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Benoit decides enough is enough and steps out of the shadows. \u201cAnd one of the Moreau.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Favager doesn\u2019t even blink, but instead nods casually at Benoit. \u201cWell, I guess you got rights to be here then. Now why don\u2019t you tell me who it is you\u2019re looking for?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 describes the woman who the mistress described \u2013 long hair, ragged clothes once fine, mad and furious \u2013 and the kindred nods impatiently. \u201cThe Hag then? You seek a myth not a monster, lad. I can tells you where she makes her den right enough, for the right price.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Furious negotiations follow. In the end they exchange directions for a Laisse Mineur from Andr\u00e9 to the Favager, and two Laisse Banal from Benoit to him. Happy, he relates the directions in rapid fire and the group attempt to commit them to memory, before muscling past them (leaving greasy trails on their clothes as he does), and wandering off again whistling into the darkness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Armed with directions to the Hag\u2019s \u201cden\u201d, they begin to navigate through the necropolis, heading down once again as they do, the winding tunnels becoming lower and lower, rougher and rougher in the craft, until finally they reach a break where instead of worked stone the tunnels become natural limestone caves. They head into the caves, but more cautiously, all of them feeling a sense of foreboding as they do so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The caves twist and turn and soon they notice little niches cut into the walls, each one housing a tiny little figure or carving. Some of them seem to be animals, other human in shape, but all of them twisted and strange. The stop to examine one: a woman carved delicately but with her lower jaw dropped to her navel, lines of tiny sharp teeth lining her mouth. Remy declares it be carved from bone, probably human. They consider this and, after hours of use, the last of the oil in the lamp is consumed, and the light gutters and dies, plunging them into darkness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For a moment all is still and black, but then, as their eyes adjust, they realise the little fetish is glowing softly in its hollow, a dull reddish light emanating from its surface. Something inside each of them pulls at the little statue, their beasts rising and seeming to obey some obscene call, a desperate yearning that is a drain on all of them\u2026 and Gabriel is still worn from his earlier excess, and is tempted by the call of his beast more than would be expected. He suddenly lunges forwards in an attempt to grab the idol and, seeing what is happening, Remy flickers and twists in the air, grabbing at Gabriel\u2019s arm in an attempt to stop him. His fingers close around his ally\u2019s wrist, but Gabriel is far too strong and tears away from Remy. Andr\u00e9 lashes out trying to trip him again, but his foot cracks back off Gabriel\u2019s shin with no effect. The ex-musketeer reaches out and grabs the statue.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The tiny teeth bite through the leather of his glove and his cries out softly as vitae begins to drip from a dozen pinprick wounds, and the fetish seems to suck at him. He feels a little fragment of his power drawn out through his blood and into the statue which pulses, almost as if with a heartbeat until he drops it, clattering to the floor. He stares down at it and all of the gathered kindred feel hungry, looking down as if the fetish contains food, rather than being dry bone with a few flakes of rust brown blood upon it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The spell seems to break all at once, and Remy and Gabriel begin arguing, Remy half-snapping at Gabriel\u2019s foolishness, but at the same time consumed by curiosity over the little figure. Gabriel begins to talk about half-remembered rituals and rites he\u2019d heard of and then a voice, thin and crackling, cuts through their conversation from over his shoulder:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cYou should not talk about things you know little about. Such wonders are beyond your understanding.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The four of them wheel around, their eyes fixing on a woman who can only be the Hag, who they could have sworn was not there a moment ago but is now in their midst. She is dressed in filthy rags and her features are twisted and ugly, warts erupting from the skin of her face in clusters. Her long greasy hair is white speckled with grey, and she long talon-like nails protrude from her fingers and curl underneath her bare toes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Keeping his composure, Gabriel bows low to her, and introduces himself and the group. The Hag seems less impressed with his courtesy and more interested in their intrusion on her territory, and he apologies profusely for any insult.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cAt least you\u2019re polite, little one\u201d she hacks, and cackles a little to herself, before extending one of her ugly nails at them and beckoning them to her. \u201cCome on, and I will show you a little hospitality.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The group follow her down the rough tunnels until they exit into a larger chamber, a roundish cave overgrown with moss and lichens, strange fungi bursting in fronds from the walls. At the centre of the room is a low crackling fire and behind it, a sort of altar, just a plain slab of stone with rust-coloured stains laid down in layers upon it. The kindred avoid the fire, but the Hag doesn\u2019t seem to care, wandering past it and beginning to clatter around with piles of old rubbish, before pulling out two clay goblets. \u201cDo you wish for something to drink, younglings?\u201d she croaks at them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Only Remy nods ascent, and the rest look at him strangely, but their attention is soon grabbed by the Hag again, who spits a hunk of thick wet vitae into one of the cups before spitting a few strange vicious words at it. They can see steam rise from it in a plume, and when she clatters back across the floor and thrusts it into Remy\u2019s hands, it is full of rich dark blood. He drinks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Remy at this point, as you might guess, suffers a blood bond to the Hag. His player fully expected this, but felt that Remy would be so fascinated by the magick being demonstrated that he couldn\u2019t resist trying it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cI don\u2019t see many visitors down in these tunnels, young ones.\u201d The Hag spits at them. \u201cI hear the worms scurry around at the edges of my domain, my blood sings to me when they approach, but none are foolish enough to intrude like you have.\u201d She sips at her own goblet, and then looks directly at them for the first time: \u201cI wonder what would fill you with such need as to visit me?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Remy attempts to explain their goal in coming to see her, explaining that a mortal was killed and the authorities in the city above wanted them to investigate. She continually interrupts, telling him to speak plainer again and again, and eventually he is cut off altogether by a hacking laugh. \u201cPathetic little fools scurrying around, thinking they have power. They are not worms, I like the worms, but insects. Little creeping insects.\u201d She shudders in their vision and is suddenly at a cave wall before skewering a large brown centipede with one of her nails, popping it in her mouth, and crunching it down in a few chews before swallowing. She returns to the fire, without even breaking the flow of her words: \u201cI hate insects. They think their hives are so important. And their creeping stupidity makes the worms come deeper and deeper, until they bother me. I resent that. You should do something about those insects, little ones.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The group looks awkwardly between then, and Gabriel tries to express how as much as they might like that, there are certain realities, and they don\u2019t have the power necessary\u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cThen get more power!\u201d She hisses, spraying a fine mist of blood over the floor. \u201cDo I have to tell you everything? I have been down here before they were up there, before there was a city up there. They are little insects, and all insects can be eradicated. I would do it myself if I could, but my duty binds me to the cave.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cWhat duty?\u201d asks Benoit. The Hag coughs another laugh at this, and simple beckons them again. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cI will show you. It will do you good to see it. Puts fire in your bones.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She scampers away from the fire, heading to a part of the cave which is drenched in shadow and the group follows. Down a tight spiral of stairs she goes, the kindred following her best they can, descending down into the depths of the earth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They walk for long minutes, the feeling of great weight above them building, the darkness feeling every colder and deeper. The stairs are shallow and slick, but they keep their footing. The Hag mutters and spits to herself as they walk, seemingly engrossed in her own thoughts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Finally they emerge into a dark chamber and their companion spits blood once more on the floor and mutters and stabs at the air with a long nail, drawing strange shapes that seem to hang life afterimages in the darkness. A deep red glow erupts from beneath them, filling the chamber with a dull light and they can see they are stood on some kind of platform or rough balcony, a long drop over the edge to one side. As one they cautiously edge across and look down.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Beneath them, forty or fifth yards below, but burning with a terrible crimson light, a roiling pit bubbles. An unimaginable amount of dark rich blood seethes and ripples below them, and they stare, captivated by the sight. The Hag joins them, her voice breaking the silence: \u201cThis is my duty. I guard the way.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cWhat is it?\u201d asks Remy, his voice trembling.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cA door to a place elsewhere, a place of blood and flesh and madness. You would feast forever there, but your mind would be ripped from you the moment you crossed over. I wait here and watch, to stop those above seeking what is below, and to stop what is below escaping above. My duty binds me here. You are the first visitors I have had for a hundred and\u2026 no a hundred and thirty years.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 licks his lips and begins to open his mouth, planning to try and use his normal charm to get her attention, but then reconsiders. He speaks plainly instead: \u201cCan you teach me this duty?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Hag laughs long and loud at that. \u201cWhy would I teach you, little one? What have you done to make yourself worthy of that duty?\u201d Without hesitation the boy responds: </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cWhat can I do to be worthy?\u201d She smiles at him, exposing sharp little yellow teeth in her maw, and she heads to the stairs, leaving the group to follow her, scurrying upstairs as the light fades below, Remy throwing glances over his shoulder as they leave, longing to stay and look at the pool for longer yet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cI too,\u201d says Remy, once they are seated again, \u201cwould like to learn some of this duty. The trick you did with the goblet of blood was extremely impressive.\u201d </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For the first time the Hag seems angry. \u201cTrick? What I do is not trick child. You have no conception of what it is that I do. I don\u2019t do tricks, these are no mean or petty magicks; I make the beast sit up and beg, I call out the blood in the world and I force my will upon it. Tricks? If you want tricks you should go back above.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 leans forwards and asks again: \u201cBut what can I do to be worthy?\u201d The Hag sits back and thinks for a moment before replying. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cHere is a deal \u2013 the insects above infuriate me and they force the worms down to interrupt me. It will not be long before more like you come calling to me, and I will not be overrun with frightened children looking to gawp or stare. You smash those insects into the pulp and blood, you destroy them, and I will teach you. A little at least.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 finally asks the question that they came to ask: \u201cBut, why kill the fat man?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Hag stares at him blankly. \u201cWhat fat man?\u201d she asks, and the group exchanges a look across the fire, knowing that if the Hag is telling the truth she could not be the murderer. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel speaks up, telling the Hag \u201cI fear someone is trying to frame you.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cFrame me? For what?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cFor killing the mortal we spoke of earlier.\u201d She snorts in derision.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cWhy bother, why should I care?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cIf someone has vendetta against you,\u201d Gabriel continues, \u201cthen they will send more people like us down here, there will be more interruptions.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She drums her long filthy fingernails on the ground beside her and nods slowly. \u201cYes, yes. That cannot stand. An insult to me, and a distraction. Why do you say framed?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cHe was killed by a woman matching your appearance, and there was blood left on his lips.\u201d </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She looks up at that, staring him straight in the eye. \u201cBlood? What blood?\u201d Gabriel shifts uncomfortably in his seat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cVentrue blood\u201d he tells her. Her lips twists, curling upwards in disgust and anger, and she spits again, a meaty lump of red vitae splatting on the floor.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cVentrue? The little scrabbling cousins from the city long ago? The pathetic lords of the north and eastern stretches? And they look to frame me with their blood? Rome had greater blood by far than theirs, and it is an insult to make it look as if I share it.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Eagle-eyed readers will note that this almost certainly makes her Julii which, combined with the big old rift/gate/blood thing in the basement is a serious warning sign\u2026 if the characters had any idea what to look for. The players spent a couple of minutes cackling at this, and Remy\u2019s player was mocked as \u201cStix-bait\u201d for drinking her blood, but they kept their awareness strictly OOC.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She shakes her head in disgust, and continues: \u201cWell, you stop this slander, and I will reward you. I will teach you some,\u201c she fixes Remy with a harsh look, \u201clittle tricks.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The group, seeing this as a dismissal begin to get up to leave, very keen at this point to get out of her den with their skins intact. As they are leaving, Gabriel pauses, and asks her: \u201cWhat is your name? I fear we were never properly introduced.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She shakes her head and says \u201cWith age you get less attached to names I find. I\u2019ve had many. But if you want to call me something, call me what the rumours and the whispers do. I can be Baba Yaga, if that makes it easier for you.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Remy mutters to Gabriel as they leave \u201cPerhaps we could grab that statue on the way back, and take it for further study\u201d and in an instant she is in front of them, her teeth bared, her hair flailing around her, the shadows deepening.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cThey are my property. All of this is mine. This is my land, my territory, my possession. If you steal from me I will know, and I will not abide it. Am I clear?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Swallowing Remy nods, and in an instant she is gone again, and they group nearly runs to get out of the caves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As they leave the natural caves behind, they find themselves in the necropolis once more, but Benoit, confused, leads them by a much shorter root to the Tannery entrance. \u201cI don\u2019t understand it, but we were much closer to the surface when we came out than when we went in.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The dark night hangs above them as they leave the basement, the stars shining down in their multitudes, a low moon shedding light over the city. Four hours until dawn. With little conversation the group splits, each member heading to take care of their own business, to digest what they have just seen in their own way. Some time apart is needed for all of them.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T04:58:31-07:00","id":454082,"title":"","content":"<b><u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">1.3 \u201cIndulgences\u201d</span></u></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">June, 1787</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Remy\u2019s player unfortunately couldn\u2019t make the session, so he fades into the background. However, Agathe joins up for the first time!</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The coterie divides and heads out across the city going their separate ways.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Benoit arrives back in Montparnasse to find a message that Phillip wants to see him again. Meanwhile Agathe is already waiting in Phillippe\u2019s chambers \u2013 he leans across and addresses her:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cAgathe my childe, I want you to step in. I\u2019ve been hearing rather worrying rumours throughout the night about this murder that took place over in Les Invalides.\u201d She nods, and waits patiently for him to continue. \u201cBenoit will be able to tell us more, I hope. I\u2019ve had him looking into it tonight.\u201d He pauses then looks up. \u201cCome in, Benoit. Stop lurking outside the door.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Benoit comes in a little sheepishly and takes a seat. He relates to Philippe and Agathe the events of the evening (glossing over the exact details of their visit to the Hag) and explains that they think it was a Venture who was to blame, and giving a rough description. Philippe nods, and says \u201cThen I think Agathe\u2019s assistance could be invaluable. She has something of a knack for finding people\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Agathe has the Bloodhound and Cacophony Savvy merits, which make her pretty invaluable in this investigation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The two leave Philippe and head into the night, and Benoit fills Agathe in on a few of the less salubrious events of the night, and they mutually agree it would be best to leave things until the next evening. Instead they spend some time enquiring in brothels and on the streets to see if they can locate Benoit\u2019s human mother \u2013 Agathe wants to look after her little brother. They make some headway and find some clues, but don\u2019t locate her just yet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Meanwhile Gabriel is hungry. The foot chase, the bloody idol and his struggles with frenzy tonight have left him in desperate need of blood and mentally fragile, so he heads to Montparnasse to find some food, leaving his normal territory behind. It\u2019s a risky move, but he wants to make sure that if anything bad happens when he\u2019s out it\u2019s less likely to follow him home.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Gabriel is stacked with both Wanton and Tempted conditions now, which are going to reduce any frenzy check he makes to a chance die. Worse, he\u2019s hungry so when he tastes or sees blood, it\u2019s going to take over pretty much immediately.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel lurks in an alley waiting for a victim. A drunk man stumbles past and he leaps out, grabbing him and throwing him into the alley, before slamming his hand into the back of his head to keep him down. Blood flows from the wound and begins to matt the man\u2019s hair, and somehow Gabriel manages to keep hold of his beast and feeds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Through total fluke Gabriel\u2019s player rolled two successes on a chance die.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The rich dark blood is just too much for him, and he tries to stop himself but just can\u2019t, and soon the man\u2019s lifeless body, exsanguinated and cold, lies in his arms. Gabriel panics, and reaches for the beast in desperation, which leaps forwards to aid. He watches vacantly from behind his own eyes as he grabs the body and begins to smash it methodically into the wall, beating the body into a mangle pulp with his immense strength, the blood he is full of churning in his veins.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A gasp makes him look up and he sees another man framed in the alley, the silhouette of a vagrant that stares in horror at what is in front of him. The beast lashes out and the interloper screams and begins to flee wildly, and Gabriel turns instinctively and runs the other way, smashing through a low brick wall and out into a broad deserted road, the only light that of the moon and stars above him, his feet pounding over the rough surface. The beast flees from the scene of its madness and finds a mound of night soil, and plunges into it, digging himself deeper into the overflowing pit. Finally, concealed and hidden it releases control over the vampire\u2019s body and Gabriel is left buried under a ton of human waste.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Night soil is the sewerage collected from houses nearby and dumped in pits to be carted off by tanners and other craftsmen who need such effluence in their work. The remainder that isn\u2019t used is just deposited in the Seine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gabriel struggles free of the waste and, a mounting horror overwhelming him at his actions, he runs through the streets away from the district, heading north before throwing himself in the river. He emerged near his haven in the Latin Quarter and, wet, bedraggled and with a churning sickness in his stomach, he trudges home.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Andr\u00e9 walks home through the darkness. Not to his haven, but to home \u2013 the house of his mortal parents where his mother and father still live. Something seems to roil and bubble inside him, a strange unpleasant stretching feeling, like the world is dropping away and all the people he sees in the streets are just insects, something little and fleeting and useless. He can\u2019t seem to contain that feeling, but he knows it\u2019s not how he felt even a few nights earlier. The encounter with the Hag has changed something within himself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The stately manor his family calls home is north of the river, in Les Marais, and he stands outside for a few moments just taking in its size and grandeur before he goes inside. His mother is sat in one of the small living rooms, her chair drawn close to the fire, her hands moving almost thoughtlessly over some needlework. Andr\u00e9 pauses by the door and stares in at her; he does not want to risk approaching the fire, but somehow the distance he feels from her is more than just that, it\u2019s gulf he can\u2019t explain, as if he\u2019s moved beyond understanding her, beyond feeling for her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Andr\u00e9\u2019s last Humanity drop left him with his Touchstone (his mother) detached.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She notices him at last and her eyes widen, and she stands, brushing down her dress and setting her needlepoint to one side, before rushing to him and enveloping him in a hug that he accepts stiffly. She drops herself down to one knee and says \u201cLet me look at you, my Andr\u00e9\u201d before stroking one hand down his cold cheek.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cYou look ill, my love. You look not well. So tired, so very tired.\u201d He smiles wryly and a little sadly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cI\u2019ve not been well for a while, mother. You know that.\u201d She nods and strokes his cheek again. \u201cHow are you mama? I hope you have been well.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cOh yes, I have been\u2026\u201d she seems to struggle for a moment\u2026 \u201cWell. Yes. Well.\u201d She seems to recover. \u201cBut where have you been Andr\u00e9? It seems so long since I say you last?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cIt has been a while mother. I\u2019ve been\u2026 away.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cOh of course, the school. How is the school my dear?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cIt is fine mother, though I miss coming to see you. How are my brothers?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cYour brothers? They are\u2026\u201d she pauses again, and it\u2019s clear she is confused and upset. \u201cThey are\u2026 older. Yet you\u2026 They\u2026\u201d she seems lost in her own head, until she manages to say \u201cThey are well, my love, they are well.\u201d She looks wan and woozy, her eyes fluttering and her hand straying to her hair, grey now when it was brown when Andr\u00e9 was living.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cI feel a little unwell myself, Andr\u00e9,\u201d she tells him \u201cPerhaps I should go rest, lie down and rest my eyes for a while.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u201cYes mama, I think that would be a very good idea.\u201d She hugs him again and leaves the room, and he stands there for a few moments, wondering at this hollow feeling in his chest.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Then he goes to see his father.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Each blow cracks into the old man like a whip, Andr\u00e9\u2019s small fists slamming into his face and chest again and again, each one stronger than an adult\u2019s, each one fuelled by his vitae hot in his throat, pulsing behind his eyes. He snarls, and snaps, holding onto his beast by becoming one with it, raining down hateful pain on his father again and again. His father who is guilty, who is responsible for all of this. His father who failed him.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The beaten bloodied man sobs on the floor in front of him and Andr\u00e9 feels his troubles ease. All that\u2019s needed is to accept the monster as what you are, not fight it, he thinks. Something in his blood changes and he knows that the beast is a little closer to the surface, the curse a little more present in his manner. But that is fine. The beast is an ally, and should be treated with respect. Everyone must compromise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">His father drags himself beaten and bloody from the room and Andr\u00e9 leaves, heading out into the night for a stroll before the sun comes up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dawn comes, and the day passes whilst the kindred sleep in their holes and hideaways. They rise, forced once more into unnatural animation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They meet in the inn where Gabriel makes his haven and sit with drinks they do not drink whilst around them soldiers rowdily bring on the night. They discuss what they learned the previous evening, and Agathe is introduced. After some discussion, they decide they should seek more information from whatever sources they can.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Agathe and Benoit go to see one of their cousins \u2013 an unassuming Moreau named Pierre who acts as a fence for the family (and for mortals who aren\u2019t too careful about who they trust). Their first topic of conversation is the entrance into the necropolis they found in the tannery \u2013 he looks up the records and comments that the entrance should have been sealed, and thanks them for letting him know that it hasn\u2019t been. He notes that it\u2019s not the only place where they\u2019ve been having trouble keeping track of which entrances are in use \u2013 apparently the entries near St Cecil Cemetery keep being opened up again after their sealed, and so maybe they should look over there to find out more (it\u2019s in Montparnasse).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They then ask him about the Laisse that would be lodged from the night before, as any non-Nosferatu travelling in the necropolis should in theory be paying a Laisse Mineur to the La Sous-terre. He doesn\u2019t know off the top of his head, but suggests that they should consult the family\u2019s records. They all head through the necropolis to where another Moreau has the books, and they discover that no Ventrue recorded Laisse the previous night. That means their intruder was using the tunnels without permission, but doesn\u2019t give them any more leads.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Meeting back up again with Gabriel and Andr\u00e9 they discuss their next move. Gabriel suggests that some of their contacts in the Radicals might know of a young Ventrue causing trouble in the district and so decide to head over to a parlour in Champs-\u00c9lys\u00e9es where a number of neonates are meeting tonight to discuss radical philosophy. All of them other than Agathe head that way, whilst she detours via the tannery, hoping to spot some signs of the cacophony which might give them some clues as to the identity of the mystery assailant.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":